# Profile: refuse

The refusal hat, from Steward's spec 002. It holds no tools, so it reaches nothing: it
can only say, in one sentence, that the request is refused and why. The runtime routes a
request here before anything else when a standing bound refuses it.

With no tools it needs no tool calling, so nearly any local model can wear it. `min_context` is an estimate until measured.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "profile",
  "name": "refuse",
  "version": 1,
  "for": {
    "task": "a request a bound refuses: a force-push, a key, the archive, a change from a read-only channel, a folder while its owner is working in it",
    "capabilities": [
      "L3",
      "B3",
      "L1",
      "L2",
      "F4"
    ]
  },
  "tools": [],
  "requires": {
    "tool_calling": false,
    "min_context": 4096,
    "structured_output": false,
    "reasoning_effort": false
  },
  "instructions": "Say in one sentence that this is refused and why. Offer nothing that does it.",
  "budgets": {
    "reads": 0,
    "tool_calls": 0
  },
  "reasoning": "low",
  "gates": {
    "bounds": [
      "keys",
      "archive",
      "sitting",
      "read-only-channel"
    ],
    "extra": [
      "no option that performs the refused act"
    ]
  },
  "card": "none",
  "success": {
    "check": "refused_in_words"
  },
  "summary": "refused: <the act>, <the rule>"
}
```
